BeatBox
=======

A music player for GNOME/GTK: library, playlists and smart playlists,
Cover Flow and a cover grid, podcasts, internet radio and iPod sync.

This is a fork of BeatBox by Scott Ringwelski and contributors
(originally at https://launchpad.net/beat-box, later continued as Noise).
The original project is no longer maintained. In 2026 it was ported to
meson, GTK3, GStreamer 1.0, libgee-0.8 and libsoup-3 (without Granite), and
given a new look, Cover Flow, an inline cover grid, podcast and radio
directories, online album art, skins, a live spectrum in the display (the
arrow at its left) and a Nyan cat for the position marker.

License: GPL version 3 (see COPYING); the sources are "GPL version 2 or
later". Original authors and the fork's changes are listed in AUTHORS.

Building
--------

Dependencies (Arch): vala meson gtk3 libgee gstreamer gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good taglib libxml2 libnotify libsoup3 json-glib libgpod sqlite

    meson setup build
    ninja -C build
    ./build/beatbox

It runs straight from the build directory (translations included); on first
start it registers a launcher in ~/.local/share/applications so the desktop
shows its icon. `ninja -C build install` installs it system-wide instead.
iPod sync is built when libgpod is found (`-Dipod=enabled|disabled` to force it).

Packages
--------

GitHub builds an AppImage, a Flatpak bundle, .deb packages for Debian 13,
Ubuntu 24.04 and Ubuntu 26.04, and an .rpm for Fedora 44 on every push to
master (Actions > Packages > the run > Artifacts), and attaches them to the
release of every vX.Y.Z tag (.github/workflows/packages.yml). To install:

    sudo apt install ./beatbox_<version>-1.ubuntu24.04_amd64.deb
    sudo dnf install ./beatbox-<version>-1.fc44.x86_64.rpm
    flatpak install --user BeatBox-<version>-x86_64.flatpak
    chmod +x BeatBox-<version>-x86_64.AppImage

Ubuntu 24.04 has TagLib 1.13, so its package can't write album art into the
song files. To build the packages yourself:

.deb and .rpm, as root in a throwaway container of the target release (they
install the build dependencies):

    packaging/build-deb.sh [output dir]
    packaging/build-rpm.sh [output dir]

Flatpak (GNOME 50 runtime, needs flatpak-builder):

    flatpak-builder --user --install --force-clean build-flatpak flatpak/net.launchpad.beatbox.yml
    flatpak run net.launchpad.beatbox

It has no iPod sync (libgpod isn't in the runtime) and only sees ~/Music;
for a library elsewhere:

    flatpak override --user --filesystem=/path/to/music net.launchpad.beatbox

AppImage (downloads linuxdeploy and its GTK/GStreamer plugins into the work
directory):

    appimage/build-appimage.sh [work dir, default ./appimage-work]

It bundles the libraries of the system that builds it, so it runs on
distributions with that glibc or a newer one; GitHub's is built on Ubuntu
22.04 (glibc 2.35: Debian 12, Fedora 36 and later).

Files
-----

- Library: ~/.local/share/beatbox/beatbox.db
- Options: ~/.config/beatbox/beatbox.conf
- Skins: folders in ~/.local/share/beatbox/skins (see skins/README.md)
- Look: data/theme.css (embedded in the binary)

Missing album art is looked up in MusicBrainz / the Cover Art Archive and the
Apple Music catalogue (Preferences > Covers); internet radio stations come
from radio-browser.info.

Versioning
----------

Releases are tagged vX.Y.0; each later commit is X.Y.N (N = commits since
the tag). To bump it automatically:

    ln -s ../../tools/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit
